om2
note seed/host/container/capview.om: capset through a view parameter. The kernel can write the header (an unknown
note version is replaced by its preferred one before -22), so capset needs a writable array (error 20).
note Without that rule (mutant capset-view) this compiles and exits 34, the low byte of version 0x20080522.
fn capv t view uchar * to long
r = capset t 0 32
ret r
end
fn main to int
h = new uchar 32 0
r = capv h
ret int get h 0
end
note gate-pools: uses capset on purpose: owner=seed/host/container/check.sh new-word acceptance or refusal qualification
